  "kangra": [
    "Because Kangra sits outside the immediate Dharamshala service area, we treat every booking there as a planned trip rather than an on-call visit, which means venue and timing details are confirmed further in advance than a local Dharamshala wedding would need. Hotel and resort venues around Kangra are generally the easiest to plan around, since they tend to have a dedicated preparation room and predictable access for the team. Home functions or less conventional venues can still be accommodated, but we ask for more detail on the space itself — where the family will be getting ready, and roughly how much room is available. Wedding season timing affects Kangra bookings just as it does Dharamshala itself, so peak-month dates are worth confirming early to avoid a scheduling clash with other travelling assignments. If the Kangra celebration spans more than a single day, let us know the full schedule upfront so travel and accommodation for the artists, where relevant, can be planned as part of the same booking rather than arranged separately.",
    "Choosing a package for an Kangra wedding starts with the same questions as any booking — how many people, what level of detail for the groom, and whether the wider baraat needs full styling or a simpler coordinated look — but travel from Dharamshala adds planning time worth building in. Because the team commits to a specific date and route for a Kangra assignment, package and quantity decisions are best finalised a week or two earlier than they would be for a local wedding, giving enough time to prepare fabric and confirm the final artist count. If your Kangra celebration includes multiple functions across a short trip, a combined package covering all of them is usually more practical than booking each date separately. We're glad to talk through a realistic package once we know your approximate headcount, the venue type, and whether the wedding is a single day or a multi-day stay — share what you have so far and we'll take it from there.",
  ],
  "palampur": [
    "Palampur weddings booked from our Dharamshala base are usually planned as a single travelling assignment rather than a standard local visit, so venue and season details matter more than they would for an in-town booking. Resort and destination-style venues around Palampur often have their own preparation spaces, which we confirm with the property directly where possible, and lawn or outdoor venues need a weather-aware backup plan for the styling area. Peak wedding season brings more competing bookings across the wider Dharamshala region, so Palampur dates during busy weeks should be confirmed with more lead time than an off-season date would need. Because the team is travelling specifically for the Palampur booking, we also factor in road or transfer time when planning the arrival buffer — an earlier ceremony time generally means an earlier departure from Dharamshala. If the venue is unfamiliar to us, sharing photos or a location pin in advance helps us plan the right team size and equipment before the day itself, rather than adjusting on arrival.",
    "For a travelling Palampur booking, the right package depends on guest count just as it would locally, but travel adds one more variable worth planning around: how many functions the team needs to cover during the trip. A single-ceremony booking is the most straightforward — one date, one venue, one styling window. A multi-function Palampur trip, covering a haldi or sangeet alongside the main wedding, is usually more efficient as one combined package rather than separate bookings, since the team is already travelling from Dharamshala and can plan artist time across the full stay. Fabric and accessory choices work the same way they would for a local booking — a coordinated palette for the groom and family, reviewed against outfit references before the team departs. Because Palampur bookings involve travel, we recommend finalising the package a little earlier than you might for an in-town wedding, so fabric, artist numbers and the travel schedule can all be confirmed together rather than adjusted at short notice.",
  ],
